    "number": "03",
    "title": "Module 03: Memory Faults",
    "html": "<h2>The C Concept</h2><p>In C, memory errors are silent. Use-after-free, out-of-bounds access, double-free, memory leaks — they all produce undefined behavior. Sometimes crashes, sometimes security vulnerabilities, sometimes nothing at all.</p><p>In crunch-c, every memory fault is caught and named:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Fault</th><th>C Equivalent</th><th>crunch-c Name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Use-after-free</td><td>Undefined behavior</td><td><code>quicksand</code></td></tr><tr><td>Out-of-bounds</td><td>Buffer overflow</td><td><code>area does not exist</code></td></tr><tr><td>Double-free</td><td>Undefined behavior</td><td><code>quicksand</code></td></tr><tr><td>Memory leak</td><td>Memory leak</td><td><code>ancient weeds</code></td></tr></tbody></table>",
